```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: green
REAL_USE_CASE: Multilingual web-scale training-data teams (C4/Dolma/FineWeb pipelines) using near-dedup libraries (datatrove, text-dedup, BigCode, NeMo-Curator) with NFKC+casefold tokenizers (T5/SentencePiece nfkc_cf) — when they run production MinHash dedup before training to avoid contamination/memorization.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Real win, not microbench. 45.2% of real C4-multilingual docs (9,044/20,000) have a model-identical NFKC-twin; 34.6% [33.6%, 35.6%] survive real MinHash at T=0.8 (5-gram char shingles over production-normalized text) — i.e., production shingle-based dedup structurally misses them. Verified open seam: datatrove + text-dedup use re.compile(r'\W+',re.UNICODE) split + .lower() — NO NFKC, NO casefold (EDITORIAL_REVISION.md §5). Chair baseline confirms non-single-mode drivers (Gini=0.852; de/fr ~94.6% with zero fullwidth-ASCII).
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Scope-bound to NFKC+casefold tokenizers — raw-bytes BPE (GPT-2/Llama) inverts the gap; BERT-multilingual NFD+lower gap vanishes (EDITORIAL_REVISION.md §3); Pipeline change requires modifying default normalizer in widely-deployed OSS (datatrove/text-dedup) and re-normalizing corpora — backward-compat and compute cost; Only actionable for teams who control both dedup normalizer and tokenizer choice — hosted API users cannot apply]
RATIONALE: Packet cites EXP-0069 real-corpus measurement (21,300 C4 docs, 5 languages) with bootstrap 95% CIs (B=10,000): prevalence 45.2%, MinHash-survival 0.346 [0.336,0.356]; per-language lower bounds clear 1% gate by 51× (ar) to 997× (zh). Mechanism reframed as textbook IR §2.2 equivalence-class mismatch (Manning et al., IIR §2.2) — measurement, not novel mechanism (CONDITION 1 satisfied). Lead metric demoted 95.1% (structurally UAX#15-predicted) to supporting; operational 34.6% is headline (CONDITION 2 satisfied). Tokenizer-family scope honestly bounded (CONDITION 3 satisfied). Production code verification substantiates ≥2 codebases misaligned (CONDITION 5 satisfied). Negative result is actionable: teams using NFKC tokenizers must align dedup to NFKC+casefold; teams using raw-bytes BPE or NFD+lower are explicitly out-of-scope — guidance prevents wasted effort.
```
